WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.089
Ask where information survives between requests.

00:00:03.089 --> 00:00:07.338
Stateful local workers need routing or state-sharing
arrangements.

00:00:07.338 --> 00:00:12.294
Stateless workers can be interchangeable because
required state is elsewhere.

00:00:12.294 --> 00:00:18.601
Do not confuse this with pure functions: a stateless
request handler can read changing records and

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:19.567
write new data.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:24.008
The architecture still has state, even when workers
do not retain it.

00:00:24.008 --> 00:00:28.490
Use the chess game to compare local memory with
shared durable state.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:34.920
Stateless workers make routing and replacement
easier, but the database now carries correctness and

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.869
coordination responsibilities.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:40.311
Cookies provide request-carried identity
information.

00:00:40.311 --> 00:00:46.482
In each design, identify what is stored, who trusts
it and what happens when a component fails.
